 "sd_reconciliation": {
  "measured_sd_per_replicate_n30000": 0.2495,
  "predicted_sd_at_n2m_if_independent": 0.0306,
  "measured_sd_at_n2m_BAL": 0.0212,
  "se_BAL_over_10_reps": 0.0067,
  "nominal_95_halfwidth_BAL": 0.0131,
  "explanation": "the two figures are the SAME quantity at different n and averaging depth. MC error scales as 1/sqrt(n): 0.2495pp at n=30,000 predicts 0.0306pp at n=2,000,000, and averaging 10 replicates divides by sqrt(10) again -> ~0.0097pp SE, whose 1.96x half-width is ~0.019pp. BAL's measured SD is 0.0212pp, TIGHTER than the 0.0306pp independent-sampling prediction (ratio 0.69), because the design is PAIRED: both arms use the same per-(game,replicate) seed, so part of the MC error is common and cancels in the difference. Variance reduction below the independent prediction is the expected behaviour of common-random-numbers, not an anomaly.",
  "no_contradiction": "0.2495pp is a per-replicate SD at the FROZEN n; 0.013pp is a half-width on a MEAN of 10 replicates at n=2M. Comparing them directly would be a units error."
 }
